    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0539" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9169/3430a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-02T20:00:00-04:00">May 2, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>808. From Department and FEA. Reference your 1525, April 29.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d497-f1"/> We do not feel that presentation at this time of your
                    proposed note <pb facs="0540" n="530" xml:id="pg530"/> on Bothnian
                        traffic<anchor n="42" xml:id="d497-f2"/> would jeopardize the attainment of
                    our other objectives. It might, in fact, strengthen our position by further
                    indicating to Swedes our doubts as to the advantages of the War Trade Agreement
                    in view of their performance under it. You are therefore requested to present
                    the proposed note with British concurrence. [Department and FEA.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d497-f1" n="41" xml:id="d497-f1-content">
